url: 'https://github.com/SE-UP/testing_artifact_detector'
abstract: >-
  The Testing Artifact Detector is a command line tool that clones and analyses Git repositories for identifiable testing.
  
  It supports the detection of Testing of the languages Python, R and C/C++ (CMake) using a static approach, i.e. it does
  not instrument the analysed projects.

  Currently, the tool works batch based, i.e. based on an input CSV, it tries to analyse all projects and generates an output
  CSV that summarises findings.
keywords:
  - Static Testing identification
